 ### CPU-based Software Rasterizer with Orbital Camera
-CPU-based Software Rasterizer with Orbital Camera is a standalone CPU-based rendering engine that performs barycentric triangle rasterization, depth buffering (Z-buffer), and directional Lambertian shading [S3, unofficial]. It features an interactive orbital camera controlled by spherical coordinates [S3, unofficial].
+CPU-based Software Rasterizer with Orbital Camera is a standalone CPU-based rendering engine that performs barycentric triangle rasterization, depth buffering (Z-buffer), and directional Lambertian shading [S3, unofficial]. It features an interactive orbital camera controlled by spherical coordinates [S3, unofficial]. The rendering pipeline performs barycentric triangle rasterization to determine which pixels are covered by each triangle, applies depth buffering to handle visibility and occlusion, and applies directional Lambertian shading to compute lighting based on surface normals and a light direction [S3, unofficial].
 
